# Playwright / browser MCP

Do **not** open Playwright or call browser MCP tools (`browser_navigate`, `browser_take_screenshot`, `browser_resize`, `browser_evaluate`, etc.) as part of your default workflow.

Use them **only when the user explicitly asks**, for example:

- “Check in the browser”
- “Take a screenshot”
- “Use Playwright”
- “Verify visually at 1030px”

For routine verification without that request, prefer:

- `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run build` (when appropriate)
- Reading code and CSS
- Shell HTTP checks (`curl`) if a dev server is already running
- Asking the user to confirm in the browser when a visual check is needed

Do not launch browser automation “just to be sure” after CSS or layout changes.
